# Agent / headless-development packages for Lunchbox.
#
# These power `lunchbox dev headless`, which boots the real launcher stack in a
# GPU-less, login-session-less headless Sway so an automated agent (or a
# developer over SSH) can screenshot and drive it. See
# docs/ai/history for the design.
# One package per line, comments start with #

# Sway is what we boot headless (already in run/test, listed for standalone use).
sway

# grim: screenshot the headless virtual output via the wlr-screencopy protocol.
# Works against the pixman software buffer with no GPU and no physical display.
grim

# wtype: inject keystrokes/text via the virtual-keyboard protocol. No daemon and
# no root (unlike ydotool). Pointer taps/clicks go through `swaymsg seat cursor`,
# so no extra pointer tool is needed.
wtype

# jq: parse `swaymsg -t get_tree`/`get_outputs` JSON for structural assertions
# (which app_id is focused/fullscreen) — cheaper and less flaky than pixel diffs.
jq
